=begin
      author: Scott
        name: deadexit
        game: gemstone
        tags: safety, bigshot
    requires: Lich > 5.14.2
     version: 0.3
        note: Written with assistance from Claude (Anthropic).

  Unattended death / low-health safety net for bigshot hunts.

  bigshot's dead_man_switch() always runs while ;bigshot is active, but unless
  its profile has "Dead man's switch" (GSF only) or "Depart/rerun if dead"
  turned on, its default behavior on death is just to kill the bigshot script
  -- it leaves you connected, dead, sitting in the room. Fine if you're
  watching, but bad if you're AFK: you decay, and anyone who wanders by can
  raise/resurrect you while you're not there to say no to it.

  This script watches for you dying while ;bigshot is (or was just) running
  and quits the game outright, so an AFK session ends in a clean logout
  instead of a decaying, rezzable corpse. It also quits if your health drops
  below LOW_HEALTH_PERCENT (25%) in the same situation, so a bad streak while
  you're away gets you out of the game before it turns into a death. It
  doesn't touch bigshot's own Dead man's switch / Depart-rerun settings --
  those still fire first; this is a belt-and-suspenders exit for whatever
  bigshot leaves behind.

  Discord (0.3, 11/08): before it quits, it posts to the same webhook exp_check
  uses (webhook_url in data/exp_check.yaml), one line, always prefixed with the
  character's name:
    "Sorry, you have died because <cause of death>."
    "Game quit due to low health (22%) ... last hit: <cause>."
    "Game quit due to <reason>."      (a request from another script, see below)
  The cause comes from the last ~80 lines the game sent: the last damage that
  came with a crit describing YOU ("... 44 points of damage!" / "Strike to your
  throat removes it!"), traced back to what dealt it -- a climb fall, a creature's
  attack line, or an explosion / spell line. If nothing matches it says so and
  quotes the last few lines instead of guessing.
  Add `death: false` to data/exp_check.yaml to mute these (exp_check's setup
  window rewrites that file, so re-add it after using the setup window).

  Other scripts can ask for an exit by setting $deadexit_request to a reason
  string (Fizzleworth-lifeguard does after repeated climb falls). The Discord
  line is sent either way; the quit only happens when afk_now is on.

  A script can also set $deadexit_notice to a string for a heads-up that is not an exit
  (Fizzleworth-prep does when it holds a hunt for encumbrance): one Discord line, never a quit.
  `notice: false` in data/exp_check.yaml mutes those, separately from `death: false`.

  Gated by the UserVar afk_now, which defaults ON. When you're actually at
  the keyboard doing interactive hunting and would rather handle your own
  death or low health yourself (get rezzed, heal, keep playing), turn it off
  for the session:

    ;vars set afk_now=false

  and flip it back on before you walk away again:

    ;vars set afk_now=true

  Meant to be autostarted for every character:

    ;autostart add --global deadexit

  Usage:  ;deadexit
  Stop:   ;kill deadexit
=end

require 'json'
require 'net/http'
require 'uri'
require 'yaml'

module DeadExit
  # === config =====================================================================
  BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME    = "bigshot"
  CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS = 3
  BIGSHOT_GRACE_SECONDS  = 20 # bridges bigshot self-killing on death just before we poll
  LOW_HEALTH_PERCENT     = 25 # quit when health is strictly below this while afk
  RECENT_MAX             = 120 # game lines kept for the cause of death
  HOOK_NAME              = "deadexit-recent"
  DEATH_LINE             = /you have died/i                       # "It seems you have died, my friend."
  # Lines that are never the cause: chat, script chatter, familiar mana log, follower spam.
  NOISE                  = /\A(?:!?[A-Z]{0,4}>|\[(?:Familiar|Thoughts|Speech|Help|Group|Private|Whisper|Lich|manalog)|--- Lich:|!)|followed\.?\z|arrives, following you/i
  FALL                   = /fall to the ground below|lose your grip and fall|will not finish the climb|let go and fall/i
  ROLL                   = /\A\s*(?:AS:|CS:|SMR|SvD|d100|1d100)|\bd100\b|\bvs DS\b/i
  DAMAGE                 = /\.\.\.\s*(?:and hits for )?(\d+) points? of damage/i
  AGAINST_YOU            = /\byour\b/i                            # a crit line that describes YOU ("...to your throat...")
  # Dying drops every buff at once; those ~25 lines would push the real cause out of the buffer.
  FADE                   = /\b(?:fades?|leaves you|wanes?|departing|dissipat\w+|returns? to normal|stops shimmering|detach itself|bursts in a bright flash|feel less confident|go back to normal|lose your extra|no longer|become solid again|leaves? you|feel your extra|quickly passes|stops? shimmering)\b/i
  ATTACK                 = /\bat you[!.]?\z/i                      # "A krag yeti swings a monstrous hairy hand at you!"
  HAZARD                 = /explodes|erupts|bursts|tendrils|boils?|sucked away|scalds|lightning|flames|shatters/i

  # === the recent-lines buffer ======================================================

  # Game text without XML, or nil when it's noise.
  def self.clean(line)
    t = line.to_s.gsub(/<[^>]*>/, "").gsub("&gt;", ">").gsub("&lt;", "<").gsub("&amp;", "&").strip
    return nil if t.empty? || t =~ NOISE || t =~ FADE
    t
  end

  def self.install_hook
    DownstreamHook.remove(HOOK_NAME) rescue nil
    DownstreamHook.add(HOOK_NAME, proc { |line|
      begin
        t = DeadExit.clean(line)
        if t
          $deadexit_recent << t
          $deadexit_recent.shift while $deadexit_recent.size > RECENT_MAX
        end
      rescue StandardError
        nil
      end
      line
    })
  end

  def self.remove_hook
    DownstreamHook.remove(HOOK_NAME) rescue nil
  end

  # === cause of death ===============================================================

  # lines: cleaned game text, oldest first, ending at the death line (or now).
  # => a short sentence fragment, or nil if nothing hit us.
  def self.cause_from(lines)
    lines = lines.last(70)
    # The newest damage line whose next line is a crit describing us ("Strike to your throat removes it!").
    di = nil
    (lines.size - 1).downto(0) do |i|
      next unless lines[i] =~ DAMAGE
      nxt = lines[i + 1].to_s
      if nxt =~ AGAINST_YOU && nxt !~ DAMAGE
        di = i
        break
      end
    end
    unless di
      # No crit line aimed at us (a plain "A hit!"): fall back to the last attack on us.
      a = lines.reverse.find { |l| l =~ ATTACK || l =~ /\A(?:An?|The|Some) .+\b(?:tries to|swings|pounds|slashes|bites|claws|lunges|strikes|hurls|throws|fires|thrusts|punches|kicks|rakes|stabs|gores|grabs)\b.+ you[!.]\z/ }
      return a ? "#{a.sub(/[!.]\z/, '')} (the last attack on you; no damage line followed it)" : nil
    end
    amount = lines[di][DAMAGE, 1]
    crit   = lines[di + 1].to_s.strip
    back   = lines[[di - 10, 0].max...di].reverse
    source =
      if (f = back.find { |l| l =~ FALL })
        "a fall while climbing"
      elsif (a = back.find { |l| l =~ ATTACK })
        a.sub(/[!.]\z/, "")
      elsif (h = back.find { |l| l =~ HAZARD && l !~ ROLL })
        h.sub(/[!.]\z/, "")
      else
        (back.find { |l| l !~ ROLL } || "something unseen").sub(/[!.]\z/, "")
      end
    note = amount.to_i <= 10 ? "; only a small hit, so probably bleeding or an earlier wound" : ""
    "#{source} (last hit, #{amount} damage: \"#{crit}\"#{note})"
  end

  # Cause from the buffer, anchored at the death line when it's there.
  def self.cause_now
    lines = $deadexit_recent.dup
    di = lines.rindex { |l| l =~ DEATH_LINE }
    lines = lines[0...di] if di
    cause_from(lines)
  end

  def self.last_lines(n = 3)
    $deadexit_recent.last(n).join(" / ")[0, 400]
  end

  def self.where
    XMLData.room_title.to_s[/\[([^\]]+)/, 1].to_s.sub(/\s*-\s*\d+\z/, "").strip
  rescue StandardError
    ""
  end

  # === Discord ======================================================================

  # Same webhook as exp_check. false when there is none, it's muted, or it failed.
  def self.notify(text, mute_key = "death")
    cfg = (YAML.safe_load(File.read(File.join(DATA_DIR, "exp_check.yaml"))) rescue nil)
    cfg = {} unless cfg.is_a?(Hash)
    url = cfg["webhook_url"].to_s.strip
    return false if url.empty? || cfg[mute_key] == false
    uri = URI(url)
    return false unless uri.is_a?(URI::HTTPS)
    body = { content: "[#{Char.name}] #{text}"[0, 1800] }.to_json
    2.times do |i|
      begin
        res = Net::HTTP.start(uri.host, uri.port, use_ssl: true, open_timeout: 5, read_timeout: 5) do |http|
          http.post(uri.request_uri, body, "Content-Type" => "application/json")
        end
        return true if res.is_a?(Net::HTTPSuccess)
        echo "deadexit: webhook answered HTTP #{res.code}#{i < 1 ? ', retrying' : ''}"
      rescue StandardError => e
        echo "deadexit: webhook failed (#{e.class}: #{e.message})#{i < 1 ? ', retrying' : ''}"
      end
      sleep 2 if i < 1
    end
    false
  end

  # === helpers ====================================================================

  # afk_now defaults ON (unset counts as on). A real boolean set via
  # `;vars set afk_now=true/false` is honored directly; any other stored
  # string only counts as OFF when it's explicitly one of false/off/no/0
  # (case-insensitive) -- everything else, including unrecognized text, stays ON.
  def self.afk_now?
    value = UserVars.afk_now
    return true if value.nil?
    return value if value == true || value == false

    value.to_s !~ /\A\s*(?:0|false|off|no)\s*\z/i
  end

  # Char.percent_health divides by max_health and raises FloatDomainError on NaN
  # before the first health update arrives, so guard on a real max first.
  def self.low_health?
    return false unless Char.max_health.to_i > 0

    Char.percent_health < LOW_HEALTH_PERCENT
  end

  # Tell Discord (once per reason), then quit. The quit is retried every poll until the
  # connection drops; the message isn't.
  def self.leave(reason_key, message, quit_note)
    unless $deadexit_told[reason_key]
      $deadexit_told[reason_key] = true
      sent = notify(message)
      echo "deadexit: #{message}#{sent ? ' [Discord sent]' : ' [no Discord message sent]'}"
    end
    echo "deadexit: #{quit_note}"
    fput "quit"
  end

  # === main =======================================================================
  def self.run
    $deadexit_recent = []
    $deadexit_told   = {}
    install_hook
    echo "deadexit started! Watching for death or health below #{LOW_HEALTH_PERCENT}% while ;#{BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME} is running (afk_now defaults ON)."
    echo "Hunting interactively? ;vars set afk_now=false to stop the auto-quit."
    echo "Stop with ;kill deadexit"

    bigshot_last_seen = nil

    loop do
      bigshot_last_seen = Time.now if Script.running?(BIGSHOT_SCRIPT_NAME)
      bigshot_recently_hunting = bigshot_last_seen && (Time.now - bigshot_last_seen) < BIGSHOT_GRACE_SECONDS

      # A heads-up from another script that is NOT an exit (e.g. Fizzleworth-prep holding the hunt
      # because it's too encumbered): one Discord line, no quit, whatever afk_now says.
      if (note = $deadexit_notice)
        $deadexit_notice = nil
        sent = notify(note.to_s, "notice")
        echo "deadexit: #{note}#{sent ? ' [Discord sent]' : ''}"
      end

      # Another script asked for an exit (e.g. lifeguard after repeated climb falls).
      if (reason = $deadexit_request)
        if afk_now?
          leave(:request, "Game quit due to #{reason}.", "#{reason} and afk_now is on -- quitting.")
        elsif !$deadexit_told[:request]
          $deadexit_told[:request] = true
          sent = notify("Stopped because of #{reason} (not quitting: afk_now is off).")
          echo "deadexit: #{reason} -- afk_now is off, not quitting.#{sent ? ' [Discord sent]' : ''}"
        end
      end

      if bigshot_recently_hunting && afk_now?
        if dead?
          cause = cause_now || "I couldn't read it from the game text (last lines: #{last_lines})"
          where = self.where
          leave(:dead, "Sorry, you have died because #{cause}#{where.empty? ? '' : " -- in #{where}"}.",
                "you're dead and afk_now is on -- quitting so you don't decay or get rezzed unattended.")
        elsif low_health?
          hit = cause_now
          leave(:low_health, "Game quit due to low health (#{Char.percent_health}%)#{hit ? ", last hit: #{hit}" : ''}.",
                "health is #{Char.percent_health}% (below #{LOW_HEALTH_PERCENT}%) and afk_now is on -- quitting before it turns into a death.")
        end
      end

      sleep CHECK_INTERVAL_SECONDS
    end
  end
end

before_dying { DeadExit.remove_hook }

DeadExit.run
